<br>
Abyss is 1 for Gods/Dragons. 1 will never exceed 10% chance. (i.e. if 3 paladins want in on bp... abyss1, pally1 2-4, pally2 5-7, pally3 8-10).<br>
<br>
Can and WILL use as PRIMARY gear is the main rule in effect.<br>
<br>
Spells - Can scribe now has precidence over can scirbe later.<br>
<br>
Last Piece Rules is in effect. (this means they HAVE all the pieces except one... Not that they only WANT one piece). Rule must be proven b4 it is put into effect (i.e. show us the armor).<br>
<br>
Abyss does NOT random Epic Pieces. If the epic piece being claimed is on a Dragon/God we will NOT also include the Abyss 1 roll when passing out the additional loot. All epic pieces will be assigned to those players on the raid that have shown the most support to the guild. If a mob drops one epic piece or 10 epic pieces, none of them are randomed.<br>
<br>
We keep half of Trak's teeth and random the other half. If it is an odd number the larger half get randomed.<br>
<br>
If a situation arises not covered by these rules Abyss reserves the right to make it up on the fly =). Thanks guys.<br>
<br>
-----<br>
edit<br>
-----<br>
<br>
For extended plane raids where people are added in after the raid is in full swing, the joining people will be out of one class drop if it occurs within the first 2 hours. Meaning, you don't get to roll on loot unless 1) 2 hours has passed or 2) 1 piece for your class has dropped since you joined. So, if an item drops ten minutes after you arrive you're out. If another piece drops five minutes later you're in for that piece. If the first class piece drops 3 hours after you joined then you're in for that piece. If people are recruited in order to take down a large mob they will be IN for all the loot on that mob but still will need to abide by the class loot rules. (i.e. if you were asked to come for Cazic and he falls an hour later you're in on all cazic loot).<br>
<br>
</font><P>Aislinn Darkenwald<br>
Level 56 Druid<br>
